WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Good morning John.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.280
I love the Olympics! I Iove its internationality, I love its history,

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.140
I love a chance to celebrate with friends and I like watching humans do extraordinary things!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.520
But I also have my problems with the Olympics, for example,

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.760
they seem to have absolutely no idea how people currently consume media.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.840
Like we can talk about them banning gifs,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.040
we can talk about their "social media opening ceremony with Ryan Seacrest",

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.800
or we can talk about how it's impossible to watch the Olympics on the Internet without a cable subscription,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.500
which most young people rightly recognize as a really bad investment.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.800
But I think if the Olympic Games can correctly imagine how media works right now,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.840
there's a bigger opportunity that's being missed.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.960
The Olympics needs to understand itself and share itself as a massively parallel viewing experience with lots -

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.660
I mean tons - of different things happening all at the
same time.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:50.800
And with distribution and production costs dropping like a rock, I think that's super totally possible;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.520
all they need is a ton of new, interesting and weird events.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.460
So, here are 17 (actually 16) sports that I think, absolutely 100%,

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.480
should be added to the Olympic Games.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.700
Number 1: Sepak Takraw, a mind-bending game native to Southeast Asia,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.440
that's basically volleyball, except played without hands.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.020
Every spike, volley, serve and block is done with the head, torso and legs.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:20.000
And this game is like 90% bicycle kicks; it's so cool and I want it to be celebrated!

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.920
Number 2: Tug-of-war. Now I know this might seem a little bit silly, but in fact,

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.520
it used to be an Olympic sport a mere 100 years ago.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.780
It's a fun team sport, with simple as dirt rules, that I frankly would love watching every four years.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.460
Number 3: Wushu. You can think of this as like gymnastics, but also fighting.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:40.800
Wushu is complex, and beautiful, and difficult to understand fully, but very easy to enjoy,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.960
with both combat versions and an exhibition version.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:44.980
Number 4: Cricket!

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.280
I don't know anything about cricket, except that it's the second most popular game in the entire world,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.560
and it's not in the Olympics, and that's dumb.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.760
Number 5: Super dope secret handshakes.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:57.480
Number 6: I don't really think that battle bots is exactly the thing that I want to see,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.060
but the ability to build and operate robots that destroy other robots,

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.559
it's something that I would like to see people able to get a gold medal in.

00:02:04.559 --> 00:02:05.579
It's.....yep.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.360
Number 7: Acapella singing, which I'm probably just mentioning

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:15.060
because Peter Hollens just released a collab video that I did with him singing Hobbit drinking songs;

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.940
and it's really great, and I'm really proud of it, and there's a link in the description.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.300
Number 8: Kite fighting.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.880
Using kite strings coated in finely ground glass,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:28.560
this South Asian sport pits kite flyers against each other with the goal of cutting the other person's kite string.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.760
This sport is popular from Afghanistan to Vietnam to Brazil.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.080
Number 9: Ultrarunning.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.340
The longest race of the Olympics right now is the marathon, at just over 26 miles;

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:41.840
ultrarunners regularly race over a hundred miles, sometimes with huge elevation gains.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.480
It's one of the most remarkable things that humans do.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.420
Number 10: Cheer.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.380
Now a lot of people belittle cheerleading, but it's pretty amazing these days;

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:53.600
and I love the idea of cheer teams cheering for entire nations, rather than just schools or sports teams.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.920
Number 11: Kabbadi. It's kind of full contact tag.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.380
Each team takes turns having an attacker raid the other side:

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.760
and they have to get in there, and touch another person on the other side,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.700
and then get back across their line without getting tackled.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.300
Number 12: Parkour, obviously .

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.760
Number 13: Darts.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.360
Because it's actually really amazing and it takes no new infrastructure.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.480
Number 14: Headis.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.580
It's like table tennis, but with soccer balls and your head. It's so great.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.080
Number 15: League of Legends.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.220
Because if the Olympics doesn't get into eSports right now, they're going to lose an entire generation.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.580
And finally number 16: Mounted archery.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.460
Because if you've got this and you've got this, then you might as well have this.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.520
Yeeaaah.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.240
There are some things about the Olympics that are necessarily old-fashioned: the pageantry and the patriotism,

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.780
and I don't think it should leave those things behind,

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:42.340
but I do think that this wonderful and ancient tradition could do a lot to be more inclusive of

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.660
the marvellous cultural diversity of our species, and thanks to modern technology, I think it can be.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.919
Also, they should let us post gifs on Tumblr and Twitter because come oooooon.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.260
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.300
(awesome hobbit drinking song playing, go check it out!)

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.200
"That's what Bilbo Baggins hates!" (song lyric)

